// Code-signing identity for local builds.
//
// Debug builds that are not signed with a stable certificate fall back to
// ad-hoc signing, whose code identity changes on every rebuild. macOS then
// treats each rebuild as a brand-new application: TCC grants stop matching
// and the keychain re-prompts for every item the production app created,
// with "Always Allow" unable to stick because the identity is different
// again next time.
//
// The team ID is personal and this repository is being prepared for public
// release, so it lives in an untracked file instead. Copy
// Signing.local.xcconfig.example to Signing.local.xcconfig and fill in your
// own DEVELOPMENT_TEAM. The optional include below keeps a fresh clone
// building (ad-hoc, with the caveats above) when that file is absent.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
